urname>Heiat</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gross</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Krumholz</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Representation of the elderly, women, and minorities in heart failure clinical trials</article-title><source>Arch Intern Med</source><year>2002</year><volume>162</volume><fpage>1682</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12153370</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/archinte.162.15.1682</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Harlan</surname><given-names>WR</given-names><suffix>3rd</suffix></name><name><surname>Sandler</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name><name><surname>Lam</surname><given-names>LC</given-names></name><name><surname>Mark</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Importance of baseline functional and socioeconomic factors for participation in cardiac rehabilitation</article-title><source>Am J Cardiol</source><year>1995</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>36</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7793400</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0002-9149(99)80797-8</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Giannuzzi</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Saner</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Bjornstad</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Fioretti</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Mendes</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Cohen-Solal</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Dugmore</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Hambrecht</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><su